<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Arcadian League</h1><p class="st-meta">370 BCE – 362 BCE (approx.) · capital Megalopolis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived federation of the Arcadian cities created after Leuctra, which built Megalopolis and helped break Spartan power in the Peloponnese.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta's</a> defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Leuctra</a> in 371 BCE freed the Arcadians to act together. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lycomedes-of-mantinea">Lycomedes of Mantinea</a> and backed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>, they formed a federal state in 370 BCE, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mantinea">Mantinea</a> was refounded. A new federal capital, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/megalopolis">Megalopolis</a>, was built by uniting dozens of villages in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league had an assembly known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-thousand">Ten Thousand</a>, a federal council and magistrates, and a standing elite force, the eparitoi, paid from federal funds. It joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> in invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laconia">Laconia</a> and supported the refounding of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/messene">Messene</a>. Arcadian pride and a sense of common identity were expressed in federal coins and dedications.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Quarrels with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/elis">Elis</a> led the Arcadians to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olympia">Olympia</a>, and disputes over using the sanctuary's treasure to pay the eparitoi split the league in 363 BCE, with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mantinea">Mantinea</a> siding with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tegea">Tegea</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mantinea-362-bce">Battle of Mantinea</a> in 362 BCE left the federation broken, though <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/megalopolis">Megalopolis</a> endured.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 370 BCE – 362 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:52.34%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>370 BCE – 362 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Megalopolis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lycomedes of Mantinea</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ancient Greek (Arcadian)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arcadian Confederacy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-366&amp;focus=arcadian-league" aria-label="Arcadian League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5233 831 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Arcadian League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5553 1087L5559 1080M5553 1087L5561 1085M5553 1087L5553 1087M5553 1087L5580 1057"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5559 1080h0M5561 1085h0M5553 1087h0M5580 1057h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5553 1087h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5553 1087h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Megalopolis. <a href="/atlas?year=-366&amp;focus=arcadian-league">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

